Track 1: The Registered Letter Swallows Sand Mountain
- Story & Context: When surveyor Caleb Vance blasted the limestone road cuts above Sand Mountain in 1974, he uncovered a meteor core fused into the gears of an 1860s courthouse steeple clock. Silas Vance used the slag to cast bridge saddles for his Gibson Les Paul, running the low strings across an antique escapement wheel that ticked against the heat of a cranked Marshall stack. During their first open rehearsal in the mill yard, the resultant subsonic overtone shattered three hurricane lanterns and shook grease from the pine rafters. Silas held his bottleneck slide against the burning nickel fret, shouting into the fog: "This parcel travelled two million miles just to get returned to sender."
