Track 2: "Tell Me When the Postmaster Quits"
- Story & Context: June Calloway spent a freezing December evening inside a stranded mail car outside Gadsden, adjusting the mechanical pendulum that regulated her guitar's trembling tone with a jeweler's screwdriver. Her fingers were caked in red clay and mineral soot from hand-grinding meteor fragments into magnetic pickup mounts. She admitted to the band that she had burned a trunk full of unopened letters from her father simply to temper the steel for her slide. As the horn section swelled to match the engine’s dying hiss, she growled into the ribbon microphone: "I kept every cancelled stamp you swore would buy your way back home."
