Track 3: Caleb Vance at Coosa Bluff
- Story & Context: Decades after the mill fell silent, retired telegraph clerks at Coosa Bluff maintained that the rusted wires along the railway still resonated with a heavy orchestral chord whenever autumn gales swept the canyon. Local kids pressed their ears to the fence posts to catch the uncanny ring of dual guitars and cellos playing in locked, clockwork unison. Legend held that Vance had sealed his meteorite-plated resonator inside the abandoned postal safe to finally halt its persistent, mechanical ringing. Yet every harvest moon, the brass section seems to rumble out across the water: "The letter missed the train, but the iron remembers the strike."
